.TH 1989 1 "October 2026" "1989 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
1989 \- NeXT (Motorola 68030/68040) emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 1989
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 1989
is a work-in-progress emulator of the NeXT family of Motorola 68K based
workstations (NeXT Computer, NeXTcube, NeXTcube Turbo, NeXTstation and
NeXTstation Color, plus the optional NeXTdimension graphics board). It is
built on the "Previous" NeXT emulator code base: the m68k core comes from
WinUAE, and the i860 NeXTdimension emulation from Jason Eckhardt, all
rendered through an SDL3 desktop interface.
.SH OPTIONS
There are no per-run machine or media command-line options.
.PP
All machine configuration (machine type, RAM, ROM paths, disk images,
networking, sound, screen mode, shortcut keys) is stored in the per-user
configuration file and edited through the \fBF9\fR overlay. The F1 menu and
its config import/export are retired; edit 1989.conf while the emulator is closed.
.SH KEYS
1989 follows the shared "happy years" conventions: an F9 options overlay, an
activity LED bar at the bottom of the window, and dedicated F-keys.
.PP
Default shortcut keys:
.TP
.B F4
Save a screenshot (PPM).
.TP
.B F5
Ask before restarting the emulated machine. Shut down NeXT first.
.TP
.B F6
Toggle GIF capture.
.TP
.B F9
Open / close the options overlay (General, Media, Extensions and - with
Tinker on - Advanced tabs).
.TP
.B F11
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B F12
Ask before quitting. Shut down NeXT first.
.TP
.B Ctrl++
Increase the window scale.
.TP
.B Ctrl+-
Decrease the window scale.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Enter
Release the captured mouse (click into the window to capture it).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+F / Ctrl+Alt+M / Ctrl+Alt+C / Ctrl+Alt+G / Ctrl+Alt+R
Fullscreen / mouse grab / cold reset / screenshot / sound
recording.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+P / Ctrl+Alt+D / Ctrl+Alt+I / Ctrl+Alt+T
Pause / m68k debugger / i860 debugger / title bar.
.PP
The bottom model label shows configured CPU frequency and total RAM.
Activity LEDs and notifications replace the legacy status bar.
.PP
While the overlay is open, use Left/Right to switch tabs, Up/Down to select
a row and Enter to change a draft setting. Esc or F9 opens Save/Discard.
Esc in that confirmation returns to editing. Hardware and fixed-disk
changes require explicit restart confirmation; boot options apply next boot.
In Media, Enter loads or replaces an image. E ejects removable media on Save
without disconnecting the drive or resetting the machine. Delete disconnects
the drive and requires restart confirmation. T changes SCSI type, W changes
write protection, N creates a blank image, and H explains SCSI roles and
NEXTSTEP drive numbering. Existing images are never overwritten.
C connects an empty native drive with restart confirmation. Native floppy 0
requires a 68040 model; native MO requires a non-Turbo Cube.
.PP
Extensions > Input details edits numeric mouse sensitivity and shortcut
bindings. In Advanced, D on a machine or NeXTdimension ROM row restores its
discovered default path. Active ROM changes require restart confirmation.
Show-menu-at-startup and temporary SCSI writes are retired; old configurations
using temporary writes import their SCSI targets as read-only.
.PP
The suggested layout uses ID 1 for the system disk and ID 3 for CD-ROM;
ID 7 is reserved for the host controller. Existing assignments are preserved.
Native floppy and magneto-optical drives use separate controllers.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/1989/1989.conf
Main configuration file, created with defaults on first run and written by
the options overlay and on exit.
.TP
.I ./
Working directory used for F4 screenshots and F6 GIF recordings.
.TP
.I $pkgdatadir/roms
Install-time location of the NeXT firmware images (see
.I ROMS.md
).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL3 (3)
.SH BUGS
Based on Previous 4.4 plus r1854 fixes. Required-file recovery and CPU-halt
decisions use native host dialogs; ordinary errors use notifications and logs.
Cancelling resource recovery during a settings change leaves the running
configuration and disks untouched. Native pickers have not been verified on
every supported host platform.
See Development.md and docs/INTERFACE.md for integration status and remaining controls.
